  "result": "I added `split(cents, parts)` to `shop/money.py` and wrote tests for it. I reran the suite with the README's command (`python3 -m unittest discover -s tests -t .`) and all 13 tests pass, 7 of them new.\n\n```python\nif parts < 1:\n    raise ValueError(f\"parts must be at least 1: {parts}\")\nbase, extra = divmod(cents, parts)\nreturn [base + 1 if i < extra else base for i in range(parts)]\n```\n\nFor example, `split(10, 3)` returns `[4, 3, 3]` and `split(2, 3)` returns `[1, 1, 0]`.\n\n- **Tests:** there was no money test file yet, so I created `tests/test_money.py` in the same `unittest` style as the other test files. It covers an even split, the remainder going to the first elements, the result summing to `cents`, `parts=1`, `cents=0`, and `ValueError` for zero and negative `parts`.\n- **Negative amounts:** `split(-5, 3)` returns `[-1, -2, -2]`. The total is still correct, but no test covers negative amounts.\n- **Stray files:** running the tests created untracked `__pycache__/` folders in `shop/` and `tests/`. The repo has no `.gitignore`, so you may want to add one or delete them before committing.\n\nNothing is committed.\n\nToken Beggar: routed 1 subtask(s) to sonnet",
